# Jane's GPU-route formatting model.
#
# Derived from qwen3:4b-instruct (Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507, Apache-2.0) rather than the
# hybrid-thinking qwen3:4b. Measured on Ollama 0.33.2 / 2026-09-02: qwen3:4b's stock
# template unconditionally opens a <think> block on the assistant turn, and `think:false`
# only stops Ollama *parsing* it -- the reasoning is still generated and lands in
# message.content (131 eval tokens to answer "OK"). Overriding the template to pre-close
# the block, and even a raw-mode prompt carrying `<think>\n\n</think>\n\n` verbatim, both
# failed to suppress it. qwen3:4b-instruct is a dedicated non-thinking checkpoint and
# answers the same prompt in 2 eval tokens.
FROM qwen3:4b-instruct

# Formatting is a transformation, not a creative task: keep it close to greedy so the
# same transcript formats the same way twice and the eval baseline stays meaningful.
PARAMETER temperature 0.2
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1
